/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL
   - Daniel chapters 6-10
   Questions authored from the KJV chapter text; verse:"" left empty per spec. */
VG.registerBibleChapters("daniel", [
{n:6, name:"The Lions' Den", seal:{ref:"Daniel 6:23",verse:"Then was the king exceeding glad for him, and commanded that they should take Daniel up out of the den. So Daniel was taken up out of the den, and no manner of hurt was found upon him, because he believed in his God."}, facts:["Did you know Daniel was likely in his eighties when he was thrown to the lions? He had served in Babylon since his youth under Nebuchadnezzar, and still held high office under Darius the Mede (Daniel 6:1-3).","Did you know the thirty-day decree made prayer itself a crime? Daniel's enemies could find no fault in his work, so they criminalized his worship instead (Daniel 6:4-7).","Did you know the lions' den was sealed with the king's own signet so no one could rescue Daniel in secret? Yet Darius still rose at dawn hoping God had done what no man could (Daniel 6:17-20)."], questions:[
{q:"How many princes did Darius set over the kingdom?", options:["An hundred and twenty","Twelve","Seventy","Three hundred"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:1",verse:"It pleased Darius to set over the kingdom an hundred and twenty princes, which should be over the whole kingdom;", insight:"A hundred and twenty princes over the whole kingdom; even empires run on delegated trust."},
{q:"How many presidents did Darius set over the princes?", options:["Three","Seven","Twelve","One"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:2",verse:"And over these three presidents; of whom Daniel was first: that the princes might give accounts unto them, and the king should have no damage.", insight:"Three presidents over the princes, and Daniel first among them; order keeps a kingdom honest."},
{q:"Why was Daniel preferred above the presidents and princes?", options:["Because an excellent spirit was in him","Because he was the oldest","Because he flattered the king","Because he was a Mede"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:3",verse:"Then this Daniel was preferred above the presidents and princes, because an excellent spirit was in him; and the king thought to set him over the whole realm.", insight:"An excellent spirit lifted him; character is the surest ladder in any court."},
{q:"What fault could the presidents and princes find in Daniel?", options:["None, for he was faithful, and no error or fault was found in him","He was often late to court","He took bribes from governors","He plotted rebellion"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:4",verse:"Then the presidents and princes sought to find occasion against Daniel concerning the kingdom; but they could find none occasion nor fault; forasmuch as he was faithful, neither was there any error or fault found in him.", insight:"They searched his record and found it clean; a faithful life leaves accusers empty-handed."},
{q:"Where did Daniel's enemies decide to find fault against him?", options:["Concerning the law of his God","In his tax records","In his dealings with the Medes","In his public speeches"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:5",verse:"Then said these men, We shall not find any occasion against this Daniel, except we find it against him concerning the law of his God.", insight:"They could only attack him where his faith stood firm; make your faith your strong place, not your weak one."},
{q:"What did the royal statute forbid for thirty days?", options:["Asking a petition of any God or man, save of the king","Leaving the city of Babylon","Trading with the Persians","Speaking the Hebrew tongue"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:7",verse:"All the presidents of the kingdom, the governors, and the princes, the counsellors, and the captains, have consulted together to establish a royal statute, and to make a firm decree, that whosoever shall ask a petition of any God or man for thirty days, save of thee, O king, he shall be cast into the den of lions.", insight:"Thirty days of forced worship of a man; flattery dressed as law is still idolatry."},
{q:"What was the penalty for breaking the decree?", options:["To be cast into the den of lions","Exile from Babylon","A heavy fine of silver","Forty stripes"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:7",verse:"All the presidents of the kingdom, the governors, and the princes, the counsellors, and the captains, have consulted together to establish a royal statute, and to make a firm decree, that whosoever shall ask a petition of any God or man for thirty days, save of thee, O king, he shall be cast into the den of lions.", insight:"The den of lions waited for the faithful; fearsome penalties cannot scare a praying man."},
{q:"Why could the signed decree not be changed?", options:["According to the law of the Medes and Persians, which altereth not","Because the king's seal was lost","Because the priests forbade it","Because Darius refused to listen"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:8",verse:"Now, O king, establish the decree, and sign the writing, that it be not changed, according to the law of the Medes and Persians, which altereth not.", insight:"Even the king could not unsign his own decree; laws made in flattery become chains on the lawmaker."},
{q:"What did Daniel do when he knew the writing was signed?", options:["He went to his house and prayed, with his windows open toward Jerusalem","He fled toward Judah","He hid his prayers in secret","He pleaded with the king"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:10",verse:"Now when Daniel knew that the writing was signed, he went into his house; and his windows being open in his chamber toward Jerusalem, he kneeled upon his knees three times a day, and prayed, and gave thanks before his God, as he did aforetime.", insight:"He prayed as he did aforetime; crisis should find you doing what you always did."},
{q:"How many times a day did Daniel pray?", options:["Three times a day","Once at dawn","Seven times","At midnight only"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:10",verse:"Now when Daniel knew that the writing was signed, he went into his house; and his windows being open in his chamber toward Jerusalem, he kneeled upon his knees three times a day, and prayed, and gave thanks before his God, as he did aforetime.", insight:"Three times a day, knees on the floor; a rhythm of prayer holds when the pressure comes."},
{q:"What did the conspirators find Daniel doing?", options:["Praying and making supplication before his God","Signing the decree","Hiding in his chamber","Fleeing the city"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:11",verse:"Then these men assembled, and found Daniel praying and making supplication before his God.", insight:"They found him praying; the most predictable thing about Daniel was his devotion."},
{q:"How did the accusers describe Daniel to the king?", options:["One of the children of the captivity of Judah","A traitor from Persia","A rebel priest","A stranger from Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:13",verse:"Then answered they and said before the king, That Daniel, which is of the children of the captivity of Judah, regardeth not thee, O king, nor the decree that thou hast signed, but maketh his petition three times a day.", insight:"They named his captivity to shame him; God was about to make his name glorious."},
{q:"How did Darius feel when he heard their accusation?", options:["Sore displeased with himself","Glad at their loyalty","Angry with Daniel","Indifferent"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:14",verse:"Then the king, when he heard these words, was sore displeased with himself, and set his heart on Daniel to deliver him: and he laboured till the going down of the sun to deliver him.", insight:"Sore displeased with himself; flattery's harvest is always regret."},
{q:"How long did the king labor to deliver Daniel?", options:["Till the going down of the sun","For three days","Until midnight","For a full week"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:14",verse:"Then the king, when he heard these words, was sore displeased with himself, and set his heart on Daniel to deliver him: and he laboured till the going down of the sun to deliver him.", insight:"He labored till sunset to undo his own decree; even kings cannot outwork their mistakes without God."},
{q:"What did the men remind the king about his own law?", options:["No decree nor statute which the king establisheth may be changed","The lions must be fed first","Daniel was innocent","The decree needed witnesses"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:15",verse:"Then these men assembled unto the king, and said unto the king, Know, O king, that the law of the Medes and Persians is, That no decree nor statute which the king establisheth may be changed.", insight:"They used the king's own law against him; vanity always collects its debt."},
{q:"What did Darius say to Daniel as he was cast into the den?", options:["Thy God whom thou servest continually, he will deliver thee","Farewell, faithful servant","The law must be obeyed","Cry out and the lions may spare thee"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:16",verse:"Then the king commanded, and they brought Daniel, and cast him into the den of lions. Now the king spake and said unto Daniel, Thy God whom thou servest continually, he will deliver thee.", insight:"'Thy God whom thou servest continually'; even a pagan king could see Daniel's constancy."},
{q:"How was the den sealed for the night?", options:["A stone was laid on its mouth, sealed with the king's signet and his lords'","With an iron door and chains","With guards alone","With a wooden cover"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:17",verse:"And a stone was brought and laid upon the mouth of the den; and the king sealed it with his own signet, and with the signet of his lords; that the purpose might not be changed concerning Daniel.", insight:"Sealed with the signets of men; heaven's seal was stronger than the stone."},
{q:"How did Darius spend the night?", options:["Fasting, with no music, and his sleep went from him","Feasting with his lords","Sleeping soundly","Praying to his gods"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:18",verse:"Then the king went to his palace, and passed the night fasting: neither were instruments of musick brought before him: and his sleep went from him.", insight:"He fasted though no law commanded it; a guilty conscience keeps its own vigil."},
{q:"What did the king cry to Daniel at dawn?", options:["O Daniel, servant of the living God, is thy God able to deliver thee from the lions?","O Daniel, art thou still alive?","O Daniel, curse thy God and live","O Daniel, the decree is undone"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:20",verse:"And when he came to the den, he cried with a lamentable voice unto Daniel: and the king spake and said to Daniel, O Daniel, servant of the living God, is thy God, whom thou servest continually, able to deliver thee from the lions?", insight:"A lamentable voice at the den; hope asked its question before the sun was fully up."},
{q:"How did Daniel explain his deliverance?", options:["My God hath sent his angel, and hath shut the lions' mouths","He fought the lions himself","The lions were not hungry","A guard rescued him"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 6:22",verse:"My God hath sent his angel, and hath shut the lions mouths, that they have not hurt me: forasmuch as before him innocency was found in me; and also before thee, O king, have I done no hurt.", insight:"God sent His angel and shut the lions' mouths; heaven is nearer to the den than we think."}
]},
{n:7, name:"The Four Beasts", seal:{ref:"Daniel 7:14",verse:"And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him: his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed."}, facts:["Did you know the four beasts of Daniel 7 mirror the four kingdoms of Nebuchadnezzar's statue dream in Daniel 2? God showed the same empires to a king as glittering metal and to His prophet as ravenous beasts.","Did you know 'one like the Son of man' in Daniel 7:13 is where Jesus took His favorite title for Himself? The gospels record Him calling Himself the Son of man more than eighty times.","Did you know the Ancient of days holds court while 'thousand thousands' minister and the books are opened? Daniel saw heaven's judgment long before the beasts' end (Daniel 7:9-10)."], questions:[
{q:"In whose first year did Daniel have the dream?", options:["Belshazzar king of Babylon","Darius the Mede","Cyrus the Persian","Nebuchadnezzar"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:1",verse:"In the first year of Belshazzar king of Babylon Daniel had a dream and visions of his head upon his bed: then he wrote the dream, and told the sum of the matters.", insight:"In Belshazzar's first year the dream came; God speaks to His servants even under godless kings."},
{q:"What did Daniel see striving upon the great sea?", options:["The four winds of the heaven","A fleet of ships","A great whale","A pillar of fire"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:2",verse:"Daniel spake and said, I saw in my vision by night, and, behold, the four winds of the heaven strove upon the great sea.", insight:"Four winds strove upon the great sea; the nations churn, but God holds the vision."},
{q:"What came up from the sea?", options:["Four great beasts, diverse one from another","Twelve ships","A mountain of brass","Seven stars"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:3",verse:"And four great beasts came up from the sea, diverse one from another.", insight:"Four great beasts, each different; empires rise, but none rise alike and none rise forever."},
{q:"What was the first beast like?", options:["A lion with eagle's wings","A bear with iron claws","A leopard with four heads","A dragon with seven horns"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:4",verse:"The first was like a lion, and had eagle’s wings: I beheld till the wings thereof were plucked, and it was lifted up from the earth, and made stand upon the feet as a man, and a man’s heart was given to it.", insight:"A lion with eagle's wings, plucked and humbled; pride with wings still falls to earth."},
{q:"What did the second beast hold in its mouth?", options:["Three ribs between its teeth","A sword of brass","A golden crown","A scroll"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:5",verse:"And behold another beast, a second, like to a bear, and it raised up itself on one side, and it had three ribs in the mouth of it between the teeth of it: and they said thus unto it, Arise, devour much flesh.", insight:"Three ribs between its teeth, told to devour much flesh; some powers grow only by consuming."},
{q:"What marked the third beast, like a leopard?", options:["Four wings of a fowl and four heads","Ten horns of iron","Eyes like the eyes of man","A mouth speaking great things"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:6",verse:"After this I beheld, and lo another, like a leopard, which had upon the back of it four wings of a fowl; the beast had also four heads; and dominion was given to it.", insight:"Four wings, four heads, and dominion given; speed and division mark the conqueror's kingdom."},
{q:"What teeth did the dreadful fourth beast have?", options:["Great iron teeth","Teeth of brass","Teeth like swords","Teeth of flint"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:7",verse:"After this I saw in the night visions, and behold a fourth beast, dreadful and terrible, and strong exceedingly; and it had great iron teeth: it devoured and brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with the feet of it: and it was diverse from all the beasts that were before it; and it had ten horns.", insight:"Great iron teeth that devoured and stamped; the cruelest kingdom still answers to heaven's court."},
{q:"How many horns did the fourth beast have?", options:["Ten","Seven","Four","Twelve"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:7",verse:"After this I saw in the night visions, and behold a fourth beast, dreadful and terrible, and strong exceedingly; and it had great iron teeth: it devoured and brake in pieces, and stamped the residue with the feet of it: and it was diverse from all the beasts that were before it; and it had ten horns.", insight:"Ten horns on the dreadful beast; even counted in advance, evil cannot surprise God."},
{q:"What was unusual about the little horn?", options:["Eyes like the eyes of man, and a mouth speaking great things","Wings like an eagle","A crown of gold","Feet like polished brass"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:8",verse:"I considered the horns, and, behold, there came up among them another little horn, before whom there were three of the first horns plucked up by the roots: and, behold, in this horn were eyes like the eyes of man, and a mouth speaking great things.", insight:"Eyes like a man and a mouth speaking great things; boasting is the native language of the little horn."},
{q:"How is the Ancient of days described?", options:["Garment white as snow, hair like pure wool","Clothed in scarlet and gold","Crowned with twelve stars","Robed in darkness"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:9",verse:"I beheld till the thrones were cast down, and the Ancient of days did sit, whose garment was white as snow, and the hair of his head like the pure wool: his throne was like the fiery flame, and his wheels as burning fire.", insight:"White as snow, pure as wool; the Judge's glory is the opposite of the beasts' terror."},
{q:"What happened in the judgment scene?", options:["The judgment was set, and the books were opened","The beasts were crowned","The sea was calmed","The stars fell"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:10",verse:"A fiery stream issued and came forth from before him: thousand thousands ministered unto him, and ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him: the judgment was set, and the books were opened.", insight:"The judgment was set and the books were opened; heaven keeps records no power can shred."},
{q:"Who came with the clouds of heaven?", options:["One like the Son of man","An army of angels","The four beasts","A chariot of fire"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:13",verse:"I saw in the night visions, and, behold, one like the Son of man came with the clouds of heaven, and came to the Ancient of days, and they brought him near before him.", insight:"One like the Son of man came with the clouds; Jesus took this very title as His own."},
{q:"What was given to the Son of man?", options:["Dominion, and glory, and a kingdom","A sword and a shield","The books of judgment","Ten thousand angels"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:14",verse:"And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him: his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed.", insight:"Dominion and glory and a kingdom that shall not pass away; every other kingdom is on loan."},
{q:"Who shall serve the Son of man?", options:["All people, nations, and languages","The saints only","The kings of the earth","The angels"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:14",verse:"And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him: his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed.", insight:"All people, nations, and languages shall serve Him; the kingdom of God has no borders."},
{q:"What are the four great beasts?", options:["Four kings which shall arise out of the earth","Four angels","Four plagues","Four mountains"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:17",verse:"These great beasts, which are four, are four kings, which shall arise out of the earth.", insight:"Four kings shall arise out of the earth; beasts rise from the sea of nations, but the saints rise from God."},
{q:"Who shall take the kingdom?", options:["The saints of the most High, for ever and ever","The little horn","The kings of Persia","The mighty of Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:18",verse:"But the saints of the most High shall take the kingdom, and possess the kingdom for ever, even for ever and ever.", insight:"The saints shall take the kingdom forever; meekness inherits what might cannot hold."},
{q:"What did the little horn do to the saints?", options:["Made war with the saints, and prevailed against them","Blessed them","Taught them wisdom","Set them free"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:21",verse:"I beheld, and the same horn made war with the saints, and prevailed against them;", insight:"It made war with the saints and prevailed, for a time; suffering is real, but it is not the end of the story."},
{q:"How long were the saints given into his hand?", options:["Until a time and times and the dividing of time","For forty years","For seventy weeks","For one thousand years"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:25",verse:"And he shall speak great words against the most High, and shall wear out the saints of the most High, and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.", insight:"A time, times, and half a time; even persecution runs on God's clock."},
{q:"What will the little horn think to change?", options:["Times and laws","The seasons of harvest","The names of the stars","The courses of rivers"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:25",verse:"And he shall speak great words against the most High, and shall wear out the saints of the most High, and think to change times and laws: and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.", insight:"He would change times and laws; rebellion always aims at God's order first."},
{q:"How did Daniel respond to the vision?", options:["His cogitations troubled him, but he kept the matter in his heart","He told the king at once","He wrote it on the city walls","He forgot it by morning"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 7:28",verse:"Hitherto is the end of the matter. As for me Daniel, my cogitations much troubled me, and my countenance changed in me: but I kept the matter in my heart.", insight:"Troubled, yet he kept the matter in his heart; some visions are to be pondered, not published."}
]},
{n:8, name:"The Ram and the Goat", seal:{ref:"Daniel 8:25",verse:"And through his policy also he shall cause craft to prosper in his hand; and he shall magnify himself in his heart, and by peace shall destroy many: he shall also stand up against the Prince of princes; but he shall be broken without hand."}, facts:["Did you know Daniel 8 names its own symbols? The ram's two horns are the kings of Media and Persia, and the rough goat is the king of Greece, centuries before Alexander's empire rose (Daniel 8:20-21).","Did you know Gabriel is named in the Old Testament only here and in Daniel 9? A voice from between the banks of the Ulai ordered him to make Daniel understand the vision (Daniel 8:16).","Did you know the 'two thousand and three hundred days' of Daniel 8:14 is the longest time prophecy in Daniel? After them, the sanctuary would be cleansed."], questions:[
{q:"In whose third year did Daniel receive this vision?", options:["King Belshazzar","King Darius","King Cyrus","King Nebuchadnezzar"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:1",verse:"In the third year of the reign of king Belshazzar a vision appeared unto me, even unto me Daniel, after that which appeared unto me at the first.", insight:"The third year of Belshazzar; God gives His servant sight while the palace is still feasting."},
{q:"Where was Daniel when he saw the vision?", options:["At Shushan in the palace, by the river of Ulai","In Babylon by the Euphrates","In Jerusalem at the temple","In Persia at Ecbatana"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:2",verse:"And I saw in a vision; and it came to pass, when I saw, that I was at Shushan in the palace, which is in the province of Elam; and I saw in a vision, and I was by the river of Ulai.", insight:"At Shushan, by the river Ulai; God meets His people in the very heart of exile."},
{q:"What stood before the river?", options:["A ram which had two horns","A lion with wings","A bear with ribs","A leopard with four heads"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:3",verse:"Then I lifted up mine eyes, and saw, and, behold, there stood before the river a ram which had two horns: and the two horns were high; but one was higher than the other, and the higher came up last.", insight:"A ram with two horns stood before the river; the vision begins where the last one left off."},
{q:"What was unusual about the ram's horns?", options:["One was higher than the other, and the higher came up last","Both were broken","They were made of iron","They pointed to the ground"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:3",verse:"Then I lifted up mine eyes, and saw, and, behold, there stood before the river a ram which had two horns: and the two horns were high; but one was higher than the other, and the higher came up last.", insight:"One horn higher, and it came up last; in kingdoms, the junior partner often rises highest."},
{q:"In which directions did the ram push?", options:["Westward, and northward, and southward","Eastward only","Toward the great sea","Into the desert"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:4",verse:"I saw the ram pushing westward, and northward, and southward; so that no beasts might stand before him, neither was there any that could deliver out of his hand; but he did according to his will, and became great.", insight:"Westward, northward, southward, and none could stand before him; unchecked power feels eternal until it is not."},
{q:"What came from the west?", options:["An he goat that touched not the ground","A chariot of fire","A whirlwind","A flock of doves"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:5",verse:"And as I was considering, behold, an he goat came from the west on the face of the whole earth, and touched not the ground: and the goat had a notable horn between his eyes.", insight:"A goat that touched not the ground; swiftness itself became a weapon of judgment."},
{q:"What marked the he goat?", options:["A notable horn between his eyes","Three ribs in his mouth","Four wings on his back","Ten horns on his head"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:5",verse:"And as I was considering, behold, an he goat came from the west on the face of the whole earth, and touched not the ground: and the goat had a notable horn between his eyes.", insight:"A notable horn between his eyes; one brilliant leader can reshape the world."},
{q:"What did the goat do to the ram?", options:["Smote the ram, brake his two horns, and stamped upon him","Made peace with him","Fled before him","Joined forces with him"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:7",verse:"And I saw him come close unto the ram, and he was moved with choler against him, and smote the ram, and brake his two horns: and there was no power in the ram to stand before him, but he cast him down to the ground, and stamped upon him: and there was none that could deliver the ram out of his hand.", insight:"Moved with choler, he broke the ram's horns; empires fall to empires, and God directs them all."},
{q:"What happened when the great horn was broken?", options:["Four notable ones came up toward the four winds of heaven","The goat died","The ram rose again","The little horn appeared"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:8",verse:"Therefore the he goat waxed very great: and when he was strong, the great horn was broken; and for it came up four notable ones toward the four winds of heaven.", insight:"Four rose where one stood; no single glory holds the world for long."},
{q:"Toward which lands did the little horn grow great?", options:["Toward the south, and toward the east, and toward the pleasant land","Toward the north and the sea","Toward Egypt and Rome","Toward the mountains"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:9",verse:"And out of one of them came forth a little horn, which waxed exceeding great, toward the south, and toward the east, and toward the pleasant land.", insight:"Toward the pleasant land it waxed exceeding great; the little horn always reaches for what is holy."},
{q:"What did the little horn take away?", options:["The daily sacrifice, and the place of the sanctuary was cast down","The king's crown","The city walls","The river's waters"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:11",verse:"Yea, he magnified himself even to the prince of the host, and by him the daily sacrifice was taken away, and the place of his sanctuary was cast down.", insight:"It took away the daily sacrifice; when worship is attacked, the battle is spiritual at its core."},
{q:"How long until the sanctuary would be cleansed?", options:["Unto two thousand and three hundred days","For seventy years","For forty days","For one week"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:14",verse:"And he said unto me, Unto two thousand and three hundred days; then shall the sanctuary be cleansed.", insight:"Two thousand and three hundred days, then cleansing; desecration has an expiration date."},
{q:"Whom did the voice command to explain the vision?", options:["Gabriel","Michael","Raphael","Uriel"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:16",verse:"And I heard a man’s voice between the banks of Ulai, which called, and said, Gabriel, make this man to understand the vision.", insight:"'Gabriel, make this man to understand'; God sends His messengers to make His visions plain."},
{q:"What did Gabriel call Daniel?", options:["O son of man","O prince of Judah","O beloved prophet","O servant of the Most High"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:17",verse:"So he came near where I stood: and when he came, I was afraid, and fell upon my face: but he said unto me, Understand, O son of man: for at the time of the end shall be the vision.", insight:"'Understand, O son of man'; the visions belong to the time of the end, yet they are given to a man."},
{q:"What did Gabriel do when Daniel lay in a deep sleep?", options:["Touched him, and set him upright","Left him alone","Called the saints","Rebuked him"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:18",verse:"Now as he was speaking with me, I was in a deep sleep on my face toward the ground: but he touched me, and set me upright.", insight:"He touched him and set him upright; heaven's touch lifts what heaven's glory lays low."},
{q:"Who are the ram's two horns?", options:["The kings of Media and Persia","The kings of Egypt and Assyria","The princes of Judah","The rulers of Greece"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:20",verse:"The ram which thou sawest having two horns are the kings of Media and Persia.", insight:"Media and Persia, named plainly; God does not speak in riddles when He wants His people to know."},
{q:"Who is the rough goat?", options:["The king of Grecia","The king of Rome","The prince of Persia","The king of the north"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:21",verse:"And the rough goat is the king of Grecia: and the great horn that is between his eyes is the first king.", insight:"The king of Grecia, centuries before Alexander; prophecy names the future like history."},
{q:"What is the great horn between the goat's eyes?", options:["The first king","The high priest","The prophet","The lawgiver"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:21",verse:"And the rough goat is the king of Grecia: and the great horn that is between his eyes is the first king.", insight:"The first king; one notable horn rises, shines, and is broken in his strength."},
{q:"How shall the king of fierce countenance be broken?", options:["Without hand","By the sword","By famine","By his own people"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:25",verse:"And through his policy also he shall cause craft to prosper in his hand; and he shall magnify himself in his heart, and by peace shall destroy many: he shall also stand up against the Prince of princes; but he shall be broken without hand.", insight:"Broken without hand; no human army ends him, for God Himself closes the account."},
{q:"What happened to Daniel after the vision?", options:["He fainted, was sick certain days, then did the king's business","He fled to Jerusalem","He refused to eat","He told Belshazzar"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 8:27",verse:"And I Daniel fainted, and was sick certain days; afterward I rose up, and did the king’s business; and I was astonished at the vision, but none understood it.", insight:"He fainted, was sick, then rose and did the king's business; visions are given to servants, not spectators."}
]},
{n:9, name:"The Seventy Weeks", seal:{ref:"Daniel 9:24",verse:"Seventy weeks are determined upon thy people and upon thy holy city, to finish the transgression, and to make an end of sins, and to make reconciliation for iniquity, and to bring in everlasting righteousness, and to seal up the vision and prophecy, and to anoint the most Holy."}, facts:["Did you know Daniel's great prayer in chapter 9 is almost entirely confession? Though personally blameless, he prays 'we have sinned' throughout, owning his people's guilt as his own.","Did you know Gabriel arrived while Daniel was still speaking? 'At the beginning of thy supplications the commandment came forth,' he said, heaven answering before the amen (Daniel 9:20-23).","Did you know the seventy weeks prophecy counts down to 'Messiah the Prince'? After sixty-nine weeks the Messiah would be 'cut off, but not for himself' (Daniel 9:25-26)."], questions:[
{q:"In whose first year did Daniel understand by the books?", options:["Darius the son of Ahasuerus","Cyrus the Persian","Belshazzar","Nebuchadnezzar"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:1",verse:"In the first year of Darius the son of Ahasuerus, of the seed of the Medes, which was made king over the realm of the Chaldeans;", insight:"The first year of Darius; an old man still reading, still seeking, still praying."},
{q:"What did Daniel understand from the books?", options:["The seventy years of Jerusalem's desolations, spoken by Jeremiah","The end of Babylon","The building of the temple","The coming of Cyrus"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:2",verse:"In the first year of his reign I Daniel understood by books the number of the years, whereof the word of the LORD came to Jeremiah the prophet, that he would accomplish seventy years in the desolations of Jerusalem.", insight:"Seventy years, counted from Jeremiah's word; Scripture interpreted Scripture for Daniel."},
{q:"How did Daniel set his face to seek God?", options:["With prayer and supplications, with fasting, and sackcloth, and ashes","With songs and feasting","With a pilgrimage to Jerusalem","With offerings of gold"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:3",verse:"And I set my face unto the Lord God, to seek by prayer and supplications, with fasting, and sackcloth, and ashes:", insight:"Fasting, sackcloth, and ashes; Daniel sought God with his body as well as his heart."},
{q:"How did Daniel address God in prayer?", options:["O Lord, the great and dreadful God","O merciful Father","O King of glory","O God of our fathers"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:4",verse:"And I prayed unto the LORD my God, and made my confession, and said, O Lord, the great and dreadful God, keeping the covenant and mercy to them that love him, and to them that keep his commandments;", insight:"The great and dreadful God, keeping covenant and mercy; Daniel prayed big because his God is big."},
{q:"How did Daniel confess?", options:["We have sinned, and have committed iniquity, and have done wickedly","I am innocent of these charges","My fathers sinned, but not I","Forgive Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:5",verse:"We have sinned, and have committed iniquity, and have done wickedly, and have rebelled, even by departing from thy precepts and from thy judgments:", insight:"'We have sinned'; Daniel had no personal guilt to confess, yet he owned his people's sin as his own."},
{q:"To whom had the prophets spoken in vain?", options:["Our kings, our princes, and our fathers, and all the people of the land","The Babylonians only","The priests alone","The little children"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:6",verse:"Neither have we hearkened unto thy servants the prophets, which spake in thy name to our kings, our princes, and our fathers, and to all the people of the land.", insight:"They would not hearken to God's servants; ignoring the prophets is the road to exile."},
{q:"To whom does righteousness belong?", options:["Unto the Lord","Unto the priests","Unto the righteous remnant","Unto the law keepers"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:7",verse:"O Lord, righteousness belongeth unto thee, but unto us confusion of faces, as at this day; to the men of Judah, and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and unto all Israel, that are near, and that are far off, through all the countries whither thou hast driven them, because of their trespass that they have trespassed against thee.", insight:"Righteousness belongs to the Lord; to us belongs confusion of face. That is honest prayer."},
{q:"What belongs to the Lord our God?", options:["Mercies and forgivenesses, though we have rebelled","Wrath and judgment only","The temple and its vessels","The land of Israel"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:9",verse:"To the Lord our God belong mercies and forgivenesses, though we have rebelled against him;", insight:"Mercies and forgivenesses belong to Him, though we rebelled; His mercy is not earned by our record."},
{q:"What was poured upon Israel?", options:["The curse and the oath written in the law of Moses","Blessings without measure","The latter rain","A new covenant"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:11",verse:"Yea, all Israel have transgressed thy law, even by departing, that they might not obey thy voice; therefore the curse is poured upon us, and the oath that is written in the law of Moses the servant of God, because we have sinned against him.", insight:"The curse written in the law of Moses was poured out; God keeps His warnings as surely as His promises."},
{q:"What had Israel failed to do in their trouble?", options:["Make prayer before the LORD, and turn from their iniquities","Offer sacrifices","Flee to Egypt","Rebuild the walls"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:13",verse:"As it is written in the law of Moses, all this evil is come upon us: yet made we not our prayer before the LORD our God, that we might turn from our iniquities, and understand thy truth.", insight:"They would not pray or turn; judgment fell not for lack of warning but for lack of repentance."},
{q:"What did Daniel plead for Jerusalem?", options:["Let thine anger and thy fury be turned away from thy city Jerusalem","Let the walls fall","Let the exile continue","Let Babylon be spared"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:16",verse:"O Lord, according to all thy righteousness, I beseech thee, let thine anger and thy fury be turned away from thy city Jerusalem, thy holy mountain: because for our sins, and for the iniquities of our fathers, Jerusalem and thy people are become a reproach to all that are about us.", insight:"Turn Thine anger from Jerusalem, Thy holy mountain; Daniel loved the city he had never lived to see restored."},
{q:"On what basis did Daniel present his supplications?", options:["Not for our righteousnesses, but for thy great mercies","For our good works","For the sake of the fathers","For the temple's glory"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:18",verse:"O my God, incline thine ear, and hear; open thine eyes, and behold our desolations, and the city which is called by thy name: for we do not present our supplications before thee for our righteousnesses, but for thy great mercies.", insight:"Not for our righteousnesses but for His great mercies; every answered prayer stands on this ground."},
{q:"What was Daniel's threefold cry?", options:["O Lord, hear; O Lord, forgive; O Lord, hearken and do","Hear, remember, and return","Forgive, cleanse, and restore","Save, heal, and deliver"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:19",verse:"O Lord, hear; O Lord, forgive; O Lord, hearken and do; defer not, for thine own sake, O my God: for thy city and thy people are called by thy name.", insight:"Hear, forgive, hearken and do; and 'defer not.' Daniel prayed like a man who knew God listens."},
{q:"Who came while Daniel was still speaking in prayer?", options:["Gabriel, being caused to fly swiftly","Michael with a sword","A man in linen","An angel of the winds"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:21",verse:"Yea, whiles I was speaking in prayer, even the man Gabriel, whom I had seen in the vision at the beginning, being caused to fly swiftly, touched me about the time of the evening oblation.", insight:"Gabriel came flying swiftly, about the time of the evening oblation; heaven answers while we are still praying."},
{q:"What did Gabriel say Daniel was?", options:["Greatly beloved","A prince among men","The wisest in Babylon","A faithful scribe"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:23",verse:"At the beginning of thy supplications the commandment came forth, and I am come to shew thee; for thou art greatly beloved: therefore understand the matter, and consider the vision.", insight:"'Thou art greatly beloved'; heaven's verdict on the praying man."},
{q:"What are the seventy weeks determined to accomplish?", options:["To finish the transgression, make an end of sins, and bring in everlasting righteousness","To rebuild Babylon","To punish Persia","To end all prophecy"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:24",verse:"Seventy weeks are determined upon thy people and upon thy holy city, to finish the transgression, and to make an end of sins, and to make reconciliation for iniquity, and to bring in everlasting righteousness, and to seal up the vision and prophecy, and to anoint the most Holy.", insight:"Finish transgression, end sins, bring everlasting righteousness; the weeks point to the work of Christ."},
{q:"How many weeks from the command to restore Jerusalem unto Messiah the Prince?", options:["Seven weeks, and threescore and two weeks","Seventy weeks","Forty weeks","Twelve weeks"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:25",verse:"Know therefore and understand, that from the going forth of the commandment to restore and to build Jerusalem unto the Messiah the Prince shall be seven weeks, and threescore and two weeks: the street shall be built again, and the wall, even in troublous times.", insight:"Seven and sixty-two weeks unto Messiah the Prince; God set a countdown to the Anointed One."},
{q:"What would happen to Messiah?", options:["He shall be cut off, but not for himself","He shall reign in Jerusalem","He shall flee to Egypt","He shall build the temple"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:26",verse:"And after threescore and two weeks shall Messiah be cut off, but not for himself: and the people of the prince that shall come shall destroy the city and the sanctuary; and the end thereof shall be with a flood, and unto the end of the war desolations are determined.", insight:"Cut off, but not for Himself; the Messiah would die for others, centuries before the cross."},
{q:"What would the people of the prince do?", options:["Destroy the city and the sanctuary","Rebuild the temple","Crown the Messiah","Make peace with Rome"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:26",verse:"And after threescore and two weeks shall Messiah be cut off, but not for himself: and the people of the prince that shall come shall destroy the city and the sanctuary; and the end thereof shall be with a flood, and unto the end of the war desolations are determined.", insight:"The city and sanctuary destroyed; prophecy wept over Jerusalem long before it fell."},
{q:"What would happen in the midst of the week?", options:["He shall cause the sacrifice and the oblation to cease","The temple would be cleansed","The walls would be built","The exile would end"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 9:27",verse:"And he shall confirm the covenant with many for one week: and in the midst of the week he shall cause the sacrifice and the oblation to cease, and for the overspreading of abominations he shall make it desolate, even until the consummation, and that determined shall be poured upon the desolate.", insight:"The sacrifice caused to cease in the midst of the week; even the calendar of sorrow serves God's plan."}
]},
{n:10, name:"The Vision at Hiddekel", seal:{ref:"Daniel 10:19",verse:"And said, O man greatly beloved, fear not: peace be unto thee, be strong, yea, be strong. And when he had spoken unto me, I was strengthened, and said, Let my lord speak; for thou hast strengthened me."}, facts:["Did you know Daniel's three-week fast in chapter 10 is one of the clearest fasting models in Scripture? He ate no pleasant bread, no meat, no wine, and did not anoint himself until the weeks were fulfilled.","Did you know the messenger was delayed twenty-one days by 'the prince of the kingdom of Persia'? Daniel 10 opens a rare window on spiritual conflict behind earthly empires.","Did you know Michael is called 'your prince' in Daniel 10:21? Israel's heavenly defender appears here standing with God's messenger against Persia and Greece."], questions:[
{q:"In whose third year was the thing revealed to Daniel?", options:["Cyrus king of Persia","Darius the Mede","Belshazzar","Ahasuerus"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:1",verse:"In the third year of Cyrus king of Persia a thing was revealed unto Daniel, whose name was called Belteshazzar; and the thing was true, but the time appointed was long: and he understood the thing, and had understanding of the vision.", insight:"The third year of Cyrus; an old exile still receiving visions under a new empire."},
{q:"How long did Daniel mourn?", options:["Three full weeks","Seven days","Forty days","One year"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:2",verse:"In those days I Daniel was mourning three full weeks.", insight:"Three full weeks of mourning; some burdens are carried in prayer for weeks, not minutes."},
{q:"What did Daniel give up during those weeks?", options:["Pleasant bread, flesh, wine, and anointing himself","All food and drink","Sleep","His work for the king"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:3",verse:"I ate no pleasant bread, neither came flesh nor wine in my mouth, neither did I anoint myself at all, till three whole weeks were fulfilled.", insight:"No pleasant bread, no wine, no anointing; Daniel's fast was focused, not showy."},
{q:"By what river was Daniel standing?", options:["The great river Hiddekel","The river Ulai","The Euphrates","The Jordan"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:4",verse:"And in the four and twentieth day of the first month, as I was by the side of the great river, which is Hiddekel;", insight:"By the side of the great river Hiddekel; God often meets His servants by the water."},
{q:"How was the man in the vision clothed?", options:["In linen, with loins girded with fine gold of Uphaz","In sackcloth and ashes","In purple and scarlet","In armor of brass"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:5",verse:"Then I lifted up mine eyes, and looked, and behold a certain man clothed in linen, whose loins were girded with fine gold of Uphaz:", insight:"Clothed in linen, girded with fine gold; heaven's messengers wear glory, not rags."},
{q:"What was his face like?", options:["As the appearance of lightning","As the sun at noon","As a polished mirror","As the moon"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:6",verse:"His body also was like the beryl, and his face as the appearance of lightning, and his eyes as lamps of fire, and his arms and his feet like in colour to polished brass, and the voice of his words like the voice of a multitude.", insight:"A face like lightning, eyes like lamps of fire; glory is beautiful and terrible at once."},
{q:"What was the voice of his words like?", options:["Like the voice of a multitude","Like soft music","Like thunder alone","Like a whisper"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:6",verse:"His body also was like the beryl, and his face as the appearance of lightning, and his eyes as lamps of fire, and his arms and his feet like in colour to polished brass, and the voice of his words like the voice of a multitude.", insight:"A voice like a multitude; when heaven speaks, it does not whisper."},
{q:"Who alone saw the vision?", options:["Daniel alone","Daniel and his companions","The men of Persia","The elders of Judah"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:7",verse:"And I Daniel alone saw the vision: for the men that were with me saw not the vision; but a great quaking fell upon them, so that they fled to hide themselves.", insight:"Daniel alone saw the vision; the deepest revelations come to those set apart."},
{q:"What happened to the men with Daniel?", options:["A great quaking fell upon them, and they fled to hide","They saw it too","They mocked him","They fell asleep"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:7",verse:"And I Daniel alone saw the vision: for the men that were with me saw not the vision; but a great quaking fell upon them, so that they fled to hide themselves.", insight:"A great quaking fell on them and they fled; the nearness of glory unsettles even bystanders."},
{q:"What happened to Daniel's strength?", options:["There remained no strength in him, and his comeliness was turned into corruption","He grew stronger","He fell into a deep sleep","He was lifted into the air"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:8",verse:"Therefore I was left alone, and saw this great vision, and there remained no strength in me: for my comeliness was turned in me into corruption, and I retained no strength.", insight:"No strength remained, comeliness turned to corruption; the glory of God undoes a man before it remakes him."},
{q:"What did the touching hand do?", options:["Set him upon his knees and upon the palms of his hands","Lifted him to his feet at once","Carried him away","Struck him down"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:10",verse:"And, behold, an hand touched me, which set me upon my knees and upon the palms of my hands.", insight:"An hand touched him and set him on his knees; heaven lifts us gently, in stages."},
{q:"What did the messenger call Daniel?", options:["O Daniel, a man greatly beloved","O prince of the exile","O wise scribe","O servant of Cyrus"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:11",verse:"And he said unto me, O Daniel, a man greatly beloved, understand the words that I speak unto thee, and stand upright: for unto thee am I now sent. And when he had spoken this word unto me, I stood trembling.", insight:"'A man greatly beloved'; that is heaven's name for the praying man."},
{q:"When were Daniel's words heard?", options:["From the first day he set his heart to understand","Only after three weeks","When Gabriel arrived","At the evening oblation"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:12",verse:"Then said he unto me, Fear not, Daniel: for from the first day that thou didst set thine heart to understand, and to chasten thyself before thy God, thy words were heard, and I am come for thy words.", insight:"From the first day thy words were heard; the answer was sent before the waiting ended."},
{q:"Who withstood the messenger?", options:["The prince of the kingdom of Persia","The king of Grecia","Belshazzar's spirit","The prince of Babylon"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:13",verse:"But the prince of the kingdom of Persia withstood me one and twenty days: but, lo, Michael, one of the chief princes, came to help me; and I remained there with the kings of Persia.", insight:"The prince of Persia withstood him one and twenty days; behind earthly kingdoms, unseen battles rage."},
{q:"Who came to help the messenger?", options:["Michael, one of the chief princes","Gabriel","A legion of angels","Daniel himself"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:13",verse:"But the prince of the kingdom of Persia withstood me one and twenty days: but, lo, Michael, one of the chief princes, came to help me; and I remained there with the kings of Persia.", insight:"Michael, one of the chief princes, came to help; even angels fight beside one another."},
{q:"Why had the messenger come to Daniel?", options:["To make him understand what shall befall his people in the latter days","To take him to heaven","To rebuke his fasting","To anoint a new king"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:14",verse:"Now I am come to make thee understand what shall befall thy people in the latter days: for yet the vision is for many days.", insight:"To show what shall befall thy people in the latter days; God trusts His servants with the future."},
{q:"What touched Daniel's lips?", options:["One like the similitude of the sons of men","A burning coal","The angel's hand","A scroll"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:16",verse:"And, behold, one like the similitude of the sons of men touched my lips: then I opened my mouth, and spake, and said unto him that stood before me, O my lord, by the vision my sorrows are turned upon me, and I have retained no strength.", insight:"One like the sons of men touched his lips; the dumb were given speech to ask their questions."},
{q:"What happened when the messenger touched Daniel again?", options:["He strengthened him","He rebuked him","He took him away","He closed his eyes"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:18",verse:"Then there came again and touched me one like the appearance of a man, and he strengthened me,", insight:"Touched again, and strengthened; God's comfort is repeated until it holds."},
{q:"What words of comfort did the messenger speak?", options:["O man greatly beloved, fear not: peace be unto thee, be strong","Arise and eat","Go in peace to Babylon","Thy sins are forgiven"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:19",verse:"And said, O man greatly beloved, fear not: peace be unto thee, be strong, yea, be strong. And when he had spoken unto me, I was strengthened, and said, Let my lord speak; for thou hast strengthened me.", insight:"'Fear not, peace be unto thee, be strong, yea, be strong'; heaven's comfort comes in doubled strength."},
{q:"Who alone holds with the messenger in these things?", options:["Michael your prince","Gabriel","The saints","The kings of Persia"], a:0, ref:"Daniel 10:21",verse:"But I will shew thee that which is noted in the scripture of truth: and there is none that holdeth with me in these things, but Michael your prince.", insight:"None but Michael your prince; Israel has a defender in the heavenlies."}
]}
]);
